From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:57:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] common/crc32c: use the generic code on x86 CPUs without
 PCLMUL

Since the update to ISA-L 2.32.0, both SSE 4.2 variants call
crc32_iscsi_01. On a CPU with SSE 4.2 but without PCLMUL, the chosen
variant handles the unaligned tail of a buffer on its own. Its
fallback for buffers shorter than 16 bytes went away together with
crc32_iscsi_00. So if a buffer ends more bytes past an 8-byte boundary
than it is long, for example 3 bytes at offset 4, the length underflows
and the routine reads about 4 GiB past the buffer.

ceph-mon, ceph-mgr and librados clients then segfault in their
messenger threads right after they start or connect. This hits VMs
whose CPU model hides PCLMUL, like the x86-64-v2-AES and x86-64-v3
models of Proxmox VE. crc32_iscsi_01 uses PCLMULQDQ itself, too, which
works in such VMs only because hiding a CPUID flag does not disable the
instruction.

So use the SSE 4.2 code only if the CPU has PCLMUL as well, and the
generic table-driven code otherwise. That is slower than the SSE 4.2
code used before ISA-L 2.32.0, but correct. CPUs with PCLMUL keep using
the same code as before.

Fixes: f1ffb15b74e1 ("common: update crc32c to support ISA-L 2.32.0")
Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
---
 src/common/crc32c.cc | 8 +++-----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/common/crc32c.cc b/src/common/crc32c.cc
index f6f2998..b6df086 100644
--- a/src/common/crc32c.cc
+++ b/src/common/crc32c.cc
@@ -30,11 +30,9 @@ ceph_crc32c_func_t ceph_choose_crc32(void)
   if (ceph_arch_intel_avx512_vpclmul && ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_avx512_vpclmul_exists()) {
     return ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_avx512_vpclmul;
   }
-  if (ceph_arch_intel_sse42 && ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_exists()) {
-    if (ceph_arch_intel_pclmul) {
-      return ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_pclmul;
-    }
-    return ceph_crc32c_intel_fast;
+  // crc32_iscsi_01, which both SSE 4.2 variants use, needs PCLMUL too
+  if (ceph_arch_intel_sse42 && ceph_arch_intel_pclmul && ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_exists()) {
+    return ceph_crc32c_intel_fast_pclmul;
   }
 #elif defined(__arm__) || defined(__aarch64__)
 # if defined(HAVE_ARMV8_CRC)
